      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 S. Karger AG, Basel.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "Previous studies showed that a recombinant bacille Calmette-Guérin (rBCG) which expressed the Der p 2 of house dust mites (Der p 2 rBCG) could suppress asthmatic airway inﬂammation. There are two possible mechanisms: (1) Der p 2 rBCG elicits immune deviation from Th2 to Th1, and (2) Der p 2 rBCG induces antigen-specific regulatory T cells. However, the role of dendritic cell (DC) Der p 2 rBCG in this protective effect and in reprogramming T-cell commitment still needs to be studied."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVES",
            "content": "The aim of this study was to determine whether DCs play a central role in the Der p 2 rBCG-mediated inhibition of allergic airway inflammation."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "DCs were collected from Der p 2 rBCG-immunized mice (Der p 2 rBCG-DCs) and adoptively transferred to Der p 2-sensitized mice. The effects of DCs on airway inflammation and immune regulation were analyzed."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Adoptive transfer of DCs from Der p 2 rBCG-immunized mice suppressed asthmatic responses, including airway inﬂammation, mucin secretion and airway responsiveness. Der p 2 rBCG-DCs could effectively inhibit excessive Th2 immune responses and induced a subtype of CD4+CD25+Foxp3+ anti-specific regulatory T cells in this asthma model. Furthermore, Der p 2 rBCG immunization recruited more plasmacytoid DCs in abdominal draining lymph nodes."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "These findings suggest that DCs played a key role in Der p 2 rBCG-induced immunoregulation. Compared with BCG, Der p 2 rBCG displayed a more potent inhibitory effect on asthma responses, which may be related to the increase in plasmacytoid DC recruitment. These results improve our understanding of the cellular basis of Der p 2 BCG-mediated inhibition of asthma."
          }
        ]
      },
